[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Two Knights Defence"]
[Variation "Italian Game: Two Knights Defense, Fork Trick, 5.Bxf7+ and 5.O-O"]
[ECO "C55"]
[Character "tactical"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "fork"]
[Themes "centre-pawns,space"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "4.Nc3 Nxe4 5.Bxf7+ or 5.O-O"]
[Start "fork-trick-nc3 4...Nxe4"]

5. Bxf7+ ( 5. O-O Nxc3 { Trades the knight before White can attack it, and Black stays a pawn up. } 6. dxc3 f6 { Guards e5 with a pawn. The knight on f3 has no good square, and Black can bring the king to safety with ...Qe7 and ...Bd6 or ...g6. } ) 5... Kxf7 6. Nxe4 d5 { Takes the centre with a gain of time on the knight. The king on f7 is safe enough because White has few pieces out. } 7. Ng3 ( 7. Neg5+ Kg8 { The king tucks itself in on g8, and ...h6 next sends the knight back. } ) 7... e4 8. Ng1 Bc5 { Aims at f2. Material is level, and Black has a big centre and the two bishops. Plan: ...Qf6, ...Rf8 and ...Kg8, then use the open f-file. } *
